meta {
  name: Portitor connector
}

script:pre-request {
  // DCP (ADR 0016): every DSP request needs a fresh self-issued token from the caller's
  // STS, since a token may be used once. Here the caller is the consumer's identity from
  // scripts/dev-identities.sh (the "portitor: identities" task in VS Code): its STS
  // issues a token for the provider's DID that lets the provider read the consumer's
  // MembershipCredential. Requests to {{dsp}} get it as their Authorization header;
  // management and metadata requests do not need one.
  const url = req.getUrl();
  if (url.includes("{{dsp}}") || url.includes("/dsp/2025-1/")) {
    const axios = require("axios");
    const form = new URLSearchParams({
      grant_type: "client_credentials",
      client_id: bru.getEnvVar("consumerId"),
      client_secret: bru.getEnvVar("stsSecret"),
      audience: bru.getEnvVar("providerId"),
      bearer_access_scope: bru.getEnvVar("dcpScope"),
    });
    const answer = await axios.post(bru.getEnvVar("stsUrl"), form.toString(), {
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" },
    });
    req.setHeader("Authorization", "Bearer " + answer.data.access_token);
  }
}

docs {
  Start the demo authority and the identities first: scripts/dev-identities.sh, or the
  VS Code task "portitor: identities" (docs/TESTING.md, Debugging in VS Code). Put the
  consumer's STS client secret (target/vscode-dcp/consumer/sts-client-secret) in the
  environment's secret stsSecret, and the management key (target/vscode-management.key)
  in apiKey.
}
